      {
        "Id": "e12dc207da424599ace9c263dedc9ba8",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE  -  1st run: leave the file empty -> <project>_SHEETS.xlsx is made next to the .rvt from your Revit sheets\nThen Browse... to that Excel.  Fill SETTINGS once (project code, originator, title block).  In SHEETS type LEVEL CODE + NUMBER,\nSHEET NAME, VIEW NAME, VIEW TYPE, LEVEL, SCALE.  SAVE the Excel -> Revit updates by itself (Automatic mode).\nNew row = new sheet (+ new view).  Changed name / number = renamed / renumbered sheet.  Never doubles sheets or views.",
